# Memory bank

Project context lives under **`docs/memory/`**. After changes that affect architecture, tooling, product behavior, CI, versions, or current focus, **update the matching markdown in the same PR** as the code.

- **Full guide**: [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) (section “Memory bank”).
- **Do not** leave stale dates, package versions, or instructions that contradict the current tree.

## How to verify

- For PRs that change architecture, tooling, CI, versions, product behavior, or “current focus”: `git diff --name-only` should include at least one file under `docs/memory/` when [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) says that area is documented there — or the PR explains why no doc update is needed.
- Spot-check “as of” / snapshot dates and version numbers in edited `docs/memory/*.md` against root `package.json` and workspace `packages/*/package.json` where relevant.
- Follow the file → “update when” table in `AGENTS.md` to confirm the right `docs/memory/*.md` files were touched.
